chemas, but does not define the development manifest fields, signing domain, key-pinning representation, or how the installer selects and validates this identity. The cited metadata parser accepts only the production manifest shape and has only qualification/production signing namespaces; the cited bootstrap packager emits only production and qualification trust keys. Specify the development format and bootstrap contents, or explicitly define a compatible extension path, so independent implementations can produce and verify the same package.","evidenceReferences":["LLD §2.1–2.2 and §3.1","scripts/daemon-bundle-metadata.mjs: namespaces and readBundleManifest() require fixed v1 fields and qualification/production domains","scripts/package-daemon-bootstrap.mjs: bootstrap packaging loops only over production and qualification keys"]},{"id":"BP-2","severity":"MED","location":"LLD §2.1 — Build v2 development bundle; §8.1 — chosen alternative","message":"The chosen local build path does not explain how the exact fetched upstream commit and origin become authenticated provenance in the produced candidate. The cited candidate builder checks that its checkout HEAD matches the supplied commit, but records origin only when running under GitHub Actions; its Actions origin validator requires the commit to equal GITHUB_SHA on main or v2. The design instead requires a local exact-source build without a GitHub Actions dependency. Define the local origin verification and signed provenance inputs, including how the configured upstream and fetched branch are bound to the commit.","evidenceReferences":["LLD §2.1 preconditions/postconditions and §8.1","scripts/package-daemon-candidate.mjs: main() checks HEAD against commit; writeCandidateMetadata() calls dispatchOrigin() only when GITHUB_ACTIONS is true","scripts/package-daemon-candidate.mjs: dispatchOrigin() accepts only refs/heads/main or refs/heads/v2 with matching GITHUB_SHA"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/chosenAlternative","/citations/1","/citations/2","/citations/4","document:line:25","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/install-signed-v2-daemon-development-bundles-E20261114234b9967/S001/LLD.md"],"limitations":[],"advice":[]},{"chunkId":"install-lifecycle","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The LLD states important authentication, isolation, compatibility, and rollback requirements, but the cited installer path does not implement a development trust domain or a separate development lifecycle. As written, the installation contract cannot be met by extending only the current documented entry points.","findings":[{"id":"IL-1","severity":"HIGH","location":"LLD §2.2, “Install or update v2 development bundle”; §3.1, “Development bundle identity”; §7 Migration","message":"The required development install domain and isolation boundary are not supported by the cited installer/bootstrap design. The LLD requires a separately pinned development key, cross-domain rejection, an explicit development bootstrap, and dedicated home, state, LaunchAgent, and socket locations. However, the bundle installer and verifier accept only `production` or `qualification`, the bootstrap packages only those two trust keys, and the installer uses fixed paths under `~/.insrc` and `~/.insrc-daemon-pilot-releases`. No development entry point or configurable independent lifecycle roots are identified. Consequently a development package cannot be installed through the cited path, and using it as written cannot satisfy the no-mutation guarantee for an existing non-development installation. Specify the development bootstrap/domain and how the isolated lifecycle roots are selected and enforced before mutation.","evidenceReferences":["LLD §2.2 preconditions/postconditions and §7 migration","scripts/install-daemon-bundle.mjs: `main()` restricts domain to `qualification`/`production` and fixes release/state/trust roots under `homedir()`","scripts/verify-daemon-bundle.mjs: `main()` accepts only `production`/`qualification`; trust key is loaded from `./trust/${domain}.pem`","scripts/package-daemon-bootstrap.mjs: key packaging loops only over production and qualification","scripts/daemon-bundle-metadata.mjs: `namespaces` contains only qualification and production"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/migration","/citations/0","/citations/1","/citations/3","/citations/5","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/install-signed-v2-daemon-development-bundles-E20261114234b9967/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/v2-dev-install-234b9967.json"],"limitations":[],"advice":[]},{"chunkId":"tests-and-acceptance","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The test strategy covers the main build and lifecycle scenarios, but its acceptance mapping does not make the required assertions traceable to concrete tests. In particular, it does not explicitly prove preservation of non-development state or identify the required trust-domain rejection cases as separate assertions.","findings":[{"id":"test-mapping-coverage","severity":"MED","location":"/body/testStrategy — Test levels and Acceptance mapping","message":"The acceptance mapping reduces the requirements to two broad test descriptions without defining the assertions that prove them. `ac2` mentions cross-domain and replay refusal, but does not explicitly map tests to wrong origin/target, digest mismatch, refusal before mutation, preservation of existing non-development state, readiness/state preservation after update, or exact-predecessor offline rollback. The contract subject “Existing non-dev state untouched” is not tied to an acceptance criterion or a concrete assertion. This leaves important security and lifecycle acceptance claims difficult to verify consistently.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md §2.2: requires rejection of wrong origin/target, digest mismatch, replay before execution, and preservation/readiness or restoration on upgrade.","LLD.md §5: requires failure before mutation for existing qualification/production state and exact pinned predecessor reconciliation during offline rollback.","LLD.md §6: contract and live subjects and the `ac1`/`ac2` mapping do not enumerate those proofs."]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/testStrategy","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/install-signed-v2-daemon-development-bundles-E20261114234b9967/S001/LLD.md","LLD.md §2.1–2.2, §5–6","scripts/package-daemon-candidate.mjs","scripts/__tests__/stage-daemon-bundle.test.ts","scripts/__tests__/daemon-release-artifact.test.ts","scripts/__tests__/daemon-release-policy.test.ts"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Map each acceptance criterion to named contract/live tests and state the expected assertions, including failed input, refusal timing, and unchanged state where applicable.","The local fixture approach is plausible for deterministic provenance and trust-boundary checks; specify the disposable Apple Silicon setup and cleanup/reset assumptions for lifecycle tests so fresh install, restart, update, and offline rollback can be repeated safely."]},{"chunkId":"sequence-artifact","status":"incomplete","summary":"The sequence definition and companion source communicate the broad build-to-install handoff, but omit security-critical ordering and recovery detail: the installer appears to stage and activate without an explicit verification gate, and readiness failure/rollback is not represented. The linked HTML source was inspected, but its rendered diagram could not be visually verified because browser access was unavailable.","findings":[{"id":"SEQ-1","severity":"MED","location":"LLD §4, sequence diagram; /body/sequenceDefinition/messages[2–3]","message":"The sequence jumps from “Stage and activate in isolated account” to “Report readiness or roll back,” without showing the required verification and refusal gates before bundle execution or activation. The LLD requires authenticating the bootstrap, validating the signed manifest, origin, target, digest, and replay status before executing bundle code; it also requires readiness verification before retaining an upgrade or restoring the exact pinned predecessor. The sequence should distinguish verification from activation and make the failed-readiness rollback path explicit, so it does not imply unverified input can be activated.","evidenceReferences":["LLD §2.2 preconditions/postconditions: authenticate bootstrap and reject cross-domain signatures, wrong origin/target, digest mismatch, and replay before executing code; verify readiness or restore predecessor.","sequence-diagram.html Mermaid source: `operator->>managed: Stage and activate in isolated account`; `managed->>operator: Report readiness or roll back`."]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/sequenceDefinition","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/0","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/1","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/2","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/3","/body/companions","document:line:82","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/install-signed-v2-daemon-development-bundles-E20261114234b9967/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/install-signed-v2-daemon-development-bundles-E20261114234b9967/S001/sequence-diagram.html","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-234b9967599e56d9-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/v2-dev-install-234b9967.json","LLD §2.2 preconditions and postconditions","sequence-diagram.html Mermaid source: participants and messages"],"limitations":["Could not inspect the rendered diagram: the computer-use browser inventory reported that the browser access host was unavailable, and no local browser renderer was available. The companion HTML source and embedded Mermaid definition were inspected; visual rendering is unverified."],"advice":[]},{"chunkId":"citations-and-scope","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The LLD states important trust and isolation constraints, but its scope and refusal/recovery sections do not fully translate them into actionable boundaries and outcomes. All six cited scripts were inspected; several cited paths are described only by name and do not define the new development-specific contracts.","findings":[{"id":"scope-error-contracts","severity":"MED","location":"/body/hldContextSlice, /body/interactionWithShared, /body/errorPaths","message":"The standalone boundary declares no owned or consumed contracts, no adjacent boundaries, and no shared interactions, while the design changes the bootstrap trust roots, bundle metadata namespace, installer entry point, and managed state/lifecycle. The sole error case covers substitution or submission to a main signing gate; it does not define refusal and recovery outcomes for wrong origin/target, digest or replay failures, bootstrap trust failure, conflicting installed state, or interrupted update reconciliation. Although some checks appear in the contract preconditions, the error-path section does not specify which state is left untouched, whether retry is safe, or how the exact predecessor and sequence floor are recovered. Clarify ownership and affected shared boundaries, then define those failure outcomes so implementation and acceptance can be traced consistently.","evidenceReferences":["LLD §2.2: authenticated bootstrap, cross-domain/origin/target/digest/replay rejection, same-domain exact-predecessor recovery and sequence-floor requirements.","LLD §3.1 and `interactionWithShared`: new trust root, manifest namespace, sequence floor and installed proof are proposed, while ownership and shared interactions remain empty.","LLD §5 and `/body/errorPaths`: one substitution/main-signing error case and two terse edge-case expectations; no outcomes for bootstrap failure, wrong origin/target, digest/replay refusal, or interrupted recovery.","scripts/install-daemon-bundle.mjs: installer accepts only qualification/production and performs lifecycle work under fixed `~/.insrc` and `~/.insrc-daemon-pilot-releases` roots.","scripts/package-daemon-bootstrap.mjs and scripts/daemon-bundle-metadata.mjs: bootstrap keys and signature namespaces currently cover only production and qualification."]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/hldContextSlice","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/errorPaths","/body/openQuestions","/citations/0","/citations/1","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/5","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/install-signed-v2-daemon-development-bundles-E20261114234b9967/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/v2-dev-install-234b9967.json","scripts/install-daemon-bundle.mjs","scripts/package-daemon-bootstrap.mjs","scripts/daemon-bundle-metadata.mjs","scripts/stage-daemon-bundle.mjs","scripts/package-daemon-candidate.mjs","scripts/insrc-daemon-install.sh"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Add a concise scope/non-goals statement identifying the development bootstrap, trust metadata, and isolated lifecycle as owned surfaces, plus any existing contracts that must remain unchanged.","Expand the error table to cover each refusal gate and interrupted-update recovery, including required no-mutation guarantees, resulting state, and safe retry or rollback behavior."]},{"chunkId":"consistency","status":"incomplete","summary":"The completed chunks cover the LLD’s build provenance, install lifecycle, tests, sequence artifact, scope, errors, and citations. Their findings align across sections: the proposed development trust/install path lacks a defined format and isolated installer path; acceptance tests do not trace all required refusal and recovery guarantees; and the sequence omits explicit verification gates. I found no additional cross-section contradiction that warrants a separate finding. The diagram’s actual rendering remains unverified, so the review is incomplete.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/install-signed-v2-daemon-development-bundles-E20261114234b9967/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/v2-dev-install-234b9967.json","checkpoint completed feedback: build-provenance (BP-1, BP-2), install-lifecycle (IL-1), tests-and-acceptance (test-mapping-coverage), sequence-artifact (SEQ-1), citations-and-scope (scope-error-contracts)"],"limitations":["The sequence diagram’s rendered appearance was not verified; the sequence-artifact chunk reports that browser access was unavailable and no local browser renderer was available. Its source was inspected there, but visual rendering remains a required unverified check."],"advice":["Resolve the existing findings BP-1, BP-2, IL-1, test-mapping-coverage, SEQ-1, and scope-error-contracts together: define the development trust/bootstrap and isolated lifecycle contract, trace each security and recovery criterion to explicit assertions, and align the sequence with those gates. Avoid duplicating these issues under new finding IDs."]}],"limitations":["Could not inspect the rendered diagram: the computer-use browser inventory reported that the browser access host was unavailable, and no local browser renderer was available. The companion HTML source and embedded Mermaid definition were inspected; visual rendering is unverified.","The sequence diagram’s rendered appearance was not verified; the sequence-artifact chunk reports that browser access was unavailable and no local browser renderer was available. Its source was inspected there, but visual rendering remains a required unverified check."],"reviewer":"daemon","reviewedContentIdentity":"b03b3c791a3c9348ebfd8f118242f2d0caa77e659829283edd0f82abd3f42a22"},"finishedAt":"2026-11-14T15:59:20.840Z","publication":{"reviewId":"v2-dev-install-234b9967","attempt":1,"state":"pending"},"submitted":{"artifactPath":"/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/install-signed-v2-daemon-development-bundles-E20261114234b9967/S001/LLD.md","attempt":1},"actionId":"start-1","operation":"start","acceptedAt":"2026-11-14T15:54:49.968Z","resourceGuard":{"daemonInstance":"8a70c3fd-2a01-49f8-8569-4d6678aaee9c","openLeases":[]}}],"admissionFailures":[]}}}}
